<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="bg-canvas py-20 px-6 md:px-8">
  <div class="max-w-[640px] mx-auto">
    <h2 class="font-serif font-normal text-[2.25rem] leading-[1.15] mb-8 text-ink">Questions families ask</h2>

    <div class="divide-y divide-hair">

      <details class="group py-4">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span class="text-ink text-[.9375rem] font-medium">We're spread across countries. How do we all see the same vault if there's no cloud?</span>
          {% icon "chevron-down", "w-4 h-4 text-muted shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" %}
        </summary>
        <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed opacity-80 mt-3">
          Collator is usually set up on a device during a visit home. From there, the export feature lets you take a private copy of the vault and share it however your family already shares sensitive documents. There's no shared account or server in between, by design.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-4">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span class="text-ink text-[.9375rem] font-medium">My parents aren't very tech-savvy. Is this for them or for me?</span>
          {% icon "chevron-down", "w-4 h-4 text-muted shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" %}
        </summary>
        <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed opacity-80 mt-3">
          Either, or both. Many families set it up together: you do the organising during a visit or a call, and your parents keep the phone and the access afterwards.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-4">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span class="text-ink text-[.9375rem] font-medium">Is this a will-writing service?</span>
          {% icon "chevron-down", "w-4 h-4 text-muted shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" %}
        </summary>
        <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed opacity-80 mt-3">
          No. Collator helps you record what already exists, including wills, nominees and where things are kept. For drafting or updating a will, speak to a qualified lawyer.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-4">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span class="text-ink text-[.9375rem] font-medium">Is any of this shared with you, or with anyone else?</span>
          {% icon "chevron-down", "w-4 h-4 text-muted shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" %}
        </summary>
        <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed opacity-80 mt-3">
          No. Everything stays on the device it's entered on, and in your own backup if you enable one. Read more on our <a href="/privacy" class="text-saffron hover:text-saffron-deep transition-colors">privacy page</a>.
        </p>
      </details>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

